window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e0c9ac1b89ddeeb2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"review-gitlab-merge-requests-with-codex\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-gitlab\">使用 Codex 审查 GitLab 合并请求</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取对应文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以使用 Codex 代码审查，对 GitLab 合并请求再进行一轮高信号审查。Codex 会检查合并请求差异、遵循代码库中的指导，并发布标准的 GitLab 代码审查，重点指出严重问题。</p> <p>GitLab 支持目前处于 Beta 阶段，对所有 ChatGPT 套餐开放。Codex 集成运行在 Codex 云端。桌面应用中的 GitHub 风格代码库控件（例如 <strong>Create pull request（创建拉取请求）</strong>）不包含在此 Beta 功能中。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始前</h2> <p>请确保你已具备：</p> <ul> <li>已连接的 GitLab 账户。GitLab.com 需要完成<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001486\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">标准连接流程（需联网）</a>；自托管或 Dedicated GitLab 实例则需要进行<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001487\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区管理员模板设置（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>如果希望 Codex 遵循代码库专属的审查指导，请准备 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 文件。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"set-up-codex-code-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">设置 Codex 代码审查</h2> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-gitlab-connection-and-codex-review-identity\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gitlab-codex\">设置 GitLab 连接和 Codex 审查身份</h3> <p>对于 GitLab.com，在 ChatGPT 中<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001486\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接到 GitLab（需联网）</a>后，再于 Codex 中连接你的 GitLab 账户。对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，每位审查者都应在<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001487\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区管理员模板（需联网）</a>发布后完成连接。</p> <p>对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，请打开 <strong>Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）</strong> → <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> → <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Connectors（连接器）</strong>（需联网）</a>。工作区管理员可以让 Codex 创建服务账户，也可以保存现有服务账户的个人访问令牌。</p> <p><a id=\"let-codex-create-the-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"codex_1\">让 Codex 创建账户</h4> <p>在 <strong>Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）</strong> → <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> → <strong>Connectors（连接器）</strong>中，选择你的自托管或 Dedicated GitLab 主机 → 选择 <strong>Set up service account（设置服务账户）</strong> → <strong>Create a service account（创建服务账户）</strong>。执行设置的工作区管理员必须拥有 GitLab 实例的管理员权限。选择 <strong>Selected groups（所选群组）</strong>或 <strong>Selected projects only（仅所选项目）</strong>，指定 Codex 可以操作的范围，然后创建账户。</p> <p>选择群组会向每个选定群组授予 Developer 权限；其项目和子群组会继承此权限。选择项目则只会向你指定的单个项目授予 Developer 权限。Codex 会创建 ChatGPT Codex Connector 实例服务账户，并为其生成具有 <code>api</code> 范围的个人访问令牌。</p> <p><a id=\"use-an-existing-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_2\">使用现有账户</h4> <p>在 GitLab 中创建或选择一个服务账户，只向 Codex 应当操作的群组或项目授予 Developer 权限。在 <strong>Service accounts（服务账户）</strong>页面中选择该账户 → <strong>Manage access tokens（管理访问令牌）</strong> → <strong>Add new token（添加新令牌）</strong>，创建一个具有 <code>api</code> 范围且有效期至少还有 30 天的<a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/profile/service_accounts/#create-a-personal-access-token-for-a-service-account\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">个人访问令牌（需联网）</a>。返回 Codex，选择 <strong>Use an existing service account（使用现有服务账户）</strong>，粘贴令牌，然后选择 <strong>Save token（保存令牌）</strong>。保存时令牌会加密，之后不会再次显示。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-the-service-account-token\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_3\">管理服务账户令牌</h4> <p>工作区管理员可以在 <strong>Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）</strong> → <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> → <strong>Connectors（连接器）</strong>中管理服务账户。对于由 Codex 创建的账户，管理员可以撤销当前令牌并生成新令牌。对于现有账户，管理员可以在 Codex 中替换或移除已保存的令牌；如有需要，也可以在 GitLab 中单独撤销该令牌。只有配置了有效令牌，Codex 才能响应 GitLab 活动。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-how-gitlab-activity-reaches-codex\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gitlab-codex_1\">选择 GitLab 活动如何到达 Codex</h3> <p><a id=\"create-a-project-environment-for-coding-tasks-or-project-specific-setup\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_4\">为编码任务或项目专属设置创建项目环境</h4> <p>如果希望 Codex 为该项目编写或运行代码（例如编辑文件、提交更改或将更新推送到合并请求分支），或者审查工作依赖项目专属密钥、网络访问或设置命令，请前往 <strong>Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）</strong> → <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> → <strong>Environments（环境）</strong>，选择 GitLab 项目并创建项目环境。</p> <p>对于 GitLab.com，启用 Codex 审查也必须创建项目环境。</p> <p>创建环境时，开启 <strong>Enable Codex activity from GitLab（启用来自 GitLab 的 Codex 活动）</strong>，以安装项目 Webhook，将合并请求、评论和问题事件发送给 Codex。创建项目 Webhook 需要 Maintainer 或 Owner 权限、管理员权限，或具有项目 Webhook 管理权限的自定义角色。已签名的项目和群组 Webhook 要求 GitLab 19.0 或更高版本。对于自托管的 GitLab 19.0，请确认 <code>webhook_signing_token</code> 功能标志已启用（默认启用）；它已在 GitLab 19.1 中移除。</p> <p><a id=\"enable-activity-for-codex-reviews-for-projects-across-a-gitlab-group\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"gitlab-codex_2\">为 GitLab 群组中的多个项目启用 Codex 审查活动</h4> <p>对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，工作区管理员可以前往 <strong>Environments（环境）</strong> → <strong>GitLab activity（GitLab 活动）</strong> → <strong>Manage groups（管理群组）</strong>，为某个群组及其子群组启用 Codex 审查。Codex 会安装一个覆盖该群组全部项目的群组 Webhook。已连接的 GitLab 用户必须是群组 Owner；群组 Webhook 还要求 GitLab Premium 或 Ultimate 套餐，以及 GitLab 19.0 或更高版本。</p> <p>启用群组活动可以开展代码审查，但不会创建项目环境。如果希望根据 GitLab 事件运行编码任务（例如编辑文件、运行命令、提交更改或向合并请求推送更新），仍需创建项目环境。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-code-review-policies\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">配置代码审查策略</h3> <p>在 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/settings/code-review?provider=gitlab\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 审查设置（需联网）</a>中配置代码审查策略。选择你的代码库，然后在 <strong>Review code（审查代码）</strong>下开启 <strong>Automatic review（自动审查）</strong>。使用 <strong>Review（审查）</strong>选择哪些人的合并请求会接受审查，使用 <strong>Trigger（触发方式）</strong>选择审查运行的时机。代码库设置可以覆盖个人默认设置。</p> <p><a id=\"request-a-codex-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex_2\">请求 Codex 审查</h2> <ol> <li>在合并请求评论中提及 <code>@codex review</code>。</li> <li>等待 Codex 作出 👀 响应并发布审查结果。</li> </ol> <p>Codex 会像团队成员一样，在合并请求中发布 GitLab 讨论和备注。默认情况下，手动请求的审查可以包含 P0、P1 和 P2 级别的发现；自动审查则重点关注 P0 和 P1 级别。</p> <p><a id=\"enable-automatic-reviews\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">启用自动审查</h2> <p>要自动审查符合条件的合并请求，请在 Codex 设置中开启 <strong>Automatic reviews（自动审查）</strong>，选择 GitLab 代码库策略，然后选择触发方式：<strong>On MR open（打开合并请求时）</strong>、<strong>On every push（每次推送时）</strong>或 <strong>Smart Trigger (Experimental)（智能触发，实验性）</strong>。当合并请求事件符合该策略和触发条件时，Codex 无需 <code>@codex review</code> 评论即可运行。</p> <p>必须通过项目 Webhook 或祖先群组 Webhook 启用 GitLab 活动。对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，已配置的服务账户还必须具有向项目回写的权限。如果已配置项目环境，Codex 会使用该环境。如果祖先群组已启用活动，其下级项目会继承该活动覆盖范围。</p> <p><a id=\"customize-what-codex-reviews\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex_3\">自定义 Codex 的审查范围</h2> <p>Codex 会在代码库中查找 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 文件，并遵循适用的代码审查规则。请在离受规则约束的代码最近的文件中添加 <code>## Code Review Rules</code> 章节。必要时，可以使用 <code>###</code> 标题对相关检查进行分组。</p> <p>例如，实验报告服务可以通过以下规则，防止曝光后的行为改变对照组：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">## Code Review Rules\n\n### Experiment cohorts\n\n- Do not filter treatment comparisons on post-exposure behavior, including conversion or retention.\n  Safe path: build cohorts from assignment or exposure; report conversion as an outcome.\n</code></pre> <p>将适用于整个代码库的规则放在根目录 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 中；特定服务的规则则可以放进嵌套文件，例如 <code>services/experiment_reporting/AGENTS.md</code>。Codex 会将根目录以及更具体、适用于每个变更文件的指导结合起来，因此无关变更不必携带特定服务的上下文。</p> <p>建议先写两三条简短规则，表达审查者经常需要说明的检查要点。实用规则应当：</p> <ul> <li><strong>关注影响重大的代码库特定行为。</strong>说明需要标记的兼容性约束、数据边界或不安全副作用，并解释其重要性。</li> <li><strong>说明安全做法或例外情况。</strong>提供足够上下文，帮助 Codex 区分真正的问题和预期行为。</li> <li><strong>保持规则范围明确且长期有效。</strong>优先描述结果，不要依赖可能变化的函数名称；并将指导放在与其约束代码相近的位置。</li> <li><strong>将机械检查留给 CI。</strong>格式、Lint 和其他确定性检查不应写进代码审查规则。</li> </ul> <p>打开一个有代表性的合并请求，并使用 <code>@codex review</code> 请求审查。根据实际发现和反馈调整规则；如果某条指导产生过多噪声，就缩小其范围或删除它。</p> <p>代码审查规则用于指导 Codex，不能代替测试、分支保护或强制审批。</p> <p>如果只想让 Codex 临时关注某一方面，可以将要求写在合并请求评论中：</p> <p><code>@codex review for issues in the database migration</code></p> <p><a id=\"act-on-review-findings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">处理审查发现</h2> <p>要修复审查发现，必须配置<strong>项目环境</strong>；仅启用群组活动只能进行审查，不能运行编码任务。如果项目已经有环境，可以在合并请求中再评论，请 Codex 修复问题：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">@codex fix the P1 issue\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会以该合并请求为上下文，启动一个<a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">旧版云端聊天</a>；如果拥有相应权限，它还可以将修复推送回该分支。</p> <p><a id=\"give-codex-other-tasks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex_4\">让 Codex 执行其他任务</h2> <p>其他编码任务同样需要<strong>已配置的项目环境</strong>；仅启用群组活动只能进行审查。如果你在评论中提及 <code>@codex</code>，但没有附加 <code>review</code>，Codex 会以该合并请求为上下文启动一个<a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">旧版云端聊天</a>。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">@codex fix the CI failures\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-code-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">排查代码审查问题</h2> <p>如果 Codex 没有响应或没有发布审查结果：</p> <ul> <li>确认已选择预期的 GitLab 应用；如果使用项目专属设置，请确认该项目关联了预期的 Codex 云端环境。</li> <li>确认项目或某个祖先群组已启用活动。在 GitLab 中检查 <strong>Webhooks（Webhook）</strong> → <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/integrations/webhooks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Recent events（最近事件）</strong>（需联网）</a>，确认合并请求和备注事件均成功送达。</li> <li>对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，请确认项目或群组 Webhook 已签名、SSL 验证已启用，并且实例版本为 GitLab 19.0 或更高版本。对于自托管的 GitLab 19.0，请确认 <code>webhook_signing_token</code> 功能标志已启用；并修复因失败而被自动禁用的 Hook。</li> <li>对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，请确认现有服务账户的个人访问令牌仍有效且具有 <code>api</code> 范围。如果服务账户由 Codex 创建，请确认它已在 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 连接器设置（需联网）</a>中正确配置，并且已启用对应项目或群组。</li> <li>对于自托管或 Dedicated GitLab，请确认拥有 Developer 项目权限（或其父群组权限）的是<strong>工作区服务账户</strong>，而不只是已连接的 GitLab 用户，这样 Codex 才能发布审查和响应。成员权限可以继承；活动启用和服务账户访问权限是两项独立设置。</li> <li>确认已启用 <strong>Code review（代码审查）</strong>或 <strong>Automatic reviews（自动审查）</strong>，并且此合并请求符合代码库策略和触发条件。</li> <li>使用 <code>@codex review</code>。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"review-gitlab-merge-requests-with-codex\">Review GitLab merge requests with Codex</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use Codex code review to get another high-signal review pass on GitLab merge requests. Codex reviews the merge request diff, follows your repository guidance, and posts a standard GitLab code review focused on serious issues.</p> <p>GitLab support is in beta and is available on all ChatGPT plans. The Codex integration runs in Codex cloud. GitHub-style repository controls in the desktop app, such as <strong>Create pull request</strong>, aren't included in this beta.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Make sure you have:</p> <ul> <li>A connected GitLab account. GitLab.com requires the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001486\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">standard connection flow (online)</a>; self-managed or Dedicated GitLab instances require <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001487\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace-admin template setup (online)</a>.</li> <li>An <code>AGENTS.md</code> file if you want Codex to follow repository-specific review guidance.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"set-up-codex-code-review\">Set up Codex code review</h2> <h3 id=\"set-up-the-gitlab-connection-and-codex-review-identity\">Set up the GitLab connection and Codex review identity</h3> <p>For GitLab.com, connect your GitLab account in Codex once you've <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001486\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">connected to GitLab in ChatGPT (online)</a>. For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, each reviewer should connect after the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001487\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace-admin template (online)</a> has been published.</p> <p>For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, open <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> → <strong>Settings</strong> → <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Connectors</strong> (online)</a>. A workspace admin can let Codex create a service account or save an existing service-account personal access token.</p> <h4 id=\"let-codex-create-the-account\">Let Codex create the account</h4> <p>In <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> → <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Connectors</strong>, select the app for your self-managed or Dedicated GitLab host → select <strong>Set up service account</strong> → <strong>Create a service account</strong>. The workspace admin completing setup must have administrator access to the GitLab instance. Choose either <strong>Selected groups</strong> or <strong>Selected projects only</strong>, then select where Codex should operate and create the account. The group option grants Developer access to each chosen group, inherited by its projects and subgroups; the project option grants Developer access only to the individual projects you choose. Codex will create the ChatGPT Codex Connector instance service account with a personal access token with the <code>api</code> scope.</p> <h4 id=\"use-an-existing-account\">Use an existing account</h4> <p>In GitLab, create or choose a service account and grant it Developer access only in the groups or projects where Codex should operate. From the <strong>Service accounts</strong> page, select the account → <strong>Manage access tokens</strong> → <strong>Add new token</strong> to <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/profile/service_accounts/#create-a-personal-access-token-for-a-service-account\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">create a personal access token (online)</a> with the <code>api</code> scope and an expiration date at least 30 days away. Back in Codex, choose <strong>Use an existing service account</strong>, paste the token, and select <strong>Save token</strong>. The token is encrypted when saved and is never shown again.</p> <h4 id=\"manage-the-service-account-token\">Manage the service-account token</h4> <p>Workspace admins can manage the service account in <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> → <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Connectors</strong>. For a Codex-created account, admins can revoke the current token and generate a new one. For an existing account, admins can replace or remove the saved token in Codex and revoke it separately in GitLab if needed. Codex cannot respond to GitLab activity until a valid token is configured.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-how-gitlab-activity-reaches-codex\">Choose how GitLab activity reaches Codex</h3> <h4 id=\"create-a-project-environment-for-coding-tasks-or-project-specific-setup\">Create a project environment for coding tasks or project-specific setup</h4> <p>In <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> → <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>Environments</strong>, choose the GitLab project and create a project environment when you want Codex to write or execute code for that project—for example, to edit files, commit changes, or push updates to a merge request branch—or when a review depends on project-specific secrets, network access, or setup commands.</p> <p>For GitLab.com, a project environment is also required to enable Codex reviews.</p> <p>While creating the environment, turn on <strong>Enable Codex activity from GitLab</strong> to install the project webhook that delivers merge request, comment, and issue events to Codex. Creating the project webhook requires Maintainer or Owner access, administrator access, or a custom role that can administer project webhooks. Signed project and group webhooks require GitLab 19.0 or newer. On self-managed GitLab 19.0, confirm the <code>webhook_signing_token</code> feature flag is enabled; it is enabled by default and was removed in GitLab 19.1.</p> <h4 id=\"enable-activity-for-codex-reviews-for-projects-across-a-gitlab-group\">Enable activity for Codex reviews for projects across a GitLab group</h4> <p>For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, workspace admins can open <strong>Environments</strong> → <strong>GitLab activity</strong> → <strong>Manage groups</strong> to enable Codex reviews across a group and its subgroups. Codex will install a group webhook covering projects throughout that group. The connected GitLab user must be a group Owner, and group webhooks require GitLab Premium or Ultimate and GitLab 19.0 or newer.</p> <p>Group activity enables code reviews but does not create project environments. To run GitLab-triggered coding tasks, such as editing files, running commands, committing changes, or pushing updates to a merge request, create a project environment.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-code-review-policies\">Configure code review policies</h3> <p>Configure code review policies in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/settings/code-review?provider=gitlab\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex review settings (online)</a>. Choose your repository, then turn on <strong>Automatic review</strong> under <strong>Review code</strong>. Use <strong>Review</strong> to choose whose merge requests receive reviews and <strong>Trigger</strong> to choose when reviews run. Repository settings can override personal defaults.</p> <h2 id=\"request-a-codex-review\">Request a Codex review</h2> <ol> <li>In a merge request comment, mention <code>@codex review</code>.</li> <li>Wait for Codex to react (👀) and post a review.</li> </ol> <p>Codex posts GitLab discussions and notes on the merge request, just like a teammate would. By default, manually requested reviews can include P0, P1, and P2 findings, while automatic reviews focus on P0 and P1 findings.</p> <h2 id=\"enable-automatic-reviews\">Enable automatic reviews</h2> <p>To review qualifying merge requests automatically, turn on <strong>Automatic reviews</strong> in Codex settings, choose the GitLab repository policy, and choose a trigger: <strong>On MR open</strong>, <strong>On every push</strong>, or <strong>Smart Trigger (Experimental)</strong>. Codex runs without an <code>@codex review</code> comment when the merge request event matches that policy and trigger.</p> <p>GitLab activity must be enabled through a project webhook or an ancestor group webhook. For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, the configured service account must also have access to write back to the project. Codex uses a configured project environment when present. If an ancestor group already enables activity, descendant projects inherit that coverage.</p> <h2 id=\"customize-what-codex-reviews\">Customize what Codex reviews</h2> <p>Codex searches your repository for <code>AGENTS.md</code> files and follows the applicable code review rules. Add a <code>## Code Review Rules</code> section to the file closest to the code the rules govern. Use <code>###</code> headings to group related checks when helpful.</p> <p>For example, an experiment-reporting service can keep post-exposure behavior from changing a comparison cohort:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">## Code Review Rules\n\n### Experiment cohorts\n\n- Do not filter treatment comparisons on post-exposure behavior, including conversion or retention.\n  Safe path: build cohorts from assignment or exposure; report conversion as an outcome.\n</code></pre> <p>Put repository-wide rules in the root <code>AGENTS.md</code> and service-specific rules in a nested file, such as <code>services/experiment_reporting/AGENTS.md</code>. Codex applies the root and more-specific guidance that covers each changed file, so unrelated changes don't have to carry service-specific context.</p> <p>Start with two or three concise rules that encode checks reviewers often explain. Useful rules:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Focus on consequential, repository-specific behavior.</strong> Describe the compatibility constraint, data boundary, or unsafe side effect to flag and why it matters.</li> <li><strong>State the safe path or exception.</strong> Give Codex enough context to distinguish a real issue from expected behavior.</li> <li><strong>Keep rules scoped and durable.</strong> Prefer outcomes over function names that can change, and place guidance near the code it governs.</li> <li><strong>Leave mechanical checks in CI.</strong> Keep formatting, lint, and other deterministic checks out of review rules.</li> </ul> <p>Open a representative merge request and request a review with <code>@codex review</code>. Refine the rules based on the findings and feedback you see, and narrow or remove guidance that produces noise.</p> <p>Code review rules guide Codex; they don't replace tests, branch protections, or required approvals.</p> <p>For a one-off focus, add it to your merge request comment:</p> <p><code>@codex review for issues in the database migration</code></p> <h2 id=\"act-on-review-findings\">Act on review findings</h2> <p>Fixing review findings requires a <strong>configured project environment</strong>; group activity alone supports reviews but cannot run coding tasks. If the project has an environment, ask Codex to fix an issue in the same merge request by leaving another comment:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">@codex fix the P1 issue\n</code></pre> <p>Codex starts a <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">legacy cloud chat</a> with the merge request as context and can push a fix back to the branch when it has permission to do so.</p> <h2 id=\"give-codex-other-tasks\">Give Codex other tasks</h2> <p>Other coding tasks also require a <strong>configured project environment</strong>; group activity alone supports reviews. If you mention <code>@codex</code> in a comment with anything other than <code>review</code>, Codex starts a <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">legacy cloud chat</a> using your merge request as context.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">@codex fix the CI failures\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-code-review\">Troubleshoot code review</h2> <p>If Codex doesn't react or post a review:</p> <ul> <li>Confirm the intended GitLab app has been selected; if you use project-specific setup, confirm the project has the intended Codex cloud environment.</li> <li>Confirm activity for the project or an ancestor group. In GitLab, check <strong>Webhooks</strong> → <a href=\"https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/integrations/webhooks/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Recent events</strong> (online)</a> and verify merge request and note deliveries succeed.</li> <li>For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, confirm the project or group webhook is signed, SSL verification is enabled, and the instance is on GitLab 19.0 or newer. On self-managed GitLab 19.0, confirm the <code>webhook_signing_token</code> feature flag is enabled; repair hooks disabled automatically after failures.</li> <li>For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, confirm an existing service-account personal access token is active and has the <code>api</code> scope. If Codex created the service account, confirm it is correctly configured in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex connector settings (online)</a> and that the project or group is enabled.</li> <li>For self-managed or Dedicated GitLab, confirm the workspace service account—not just the connected GitLab user—has Developer access to the project or a parent group so Codex can post reviews and reactions. Membership is inherited; activity and service-account access are separate.</li> <li>Confirm <strong>Code review</strong> or <strong>Automatic reviews</strong> is enabled and the MR matches the repository policy and trigger.</li> <li>Use <code>@codex review</code>.</li> </ul>"};
